 "split_report": {
  "date": "2026-10-16",
  "item": "lem-cbc-grothendieck-hyperdescent-local-refinement",
  "worker": "stage1",
  "summary": "Proved the total topology is exactly the covering-shadow topology, used local lower refinements to lift each finite matching boundary to a common index, projected arbitrary total hypercovers to the target fibre and identified their coherent descent diagrams. Proved the reverse implication by fibre hypercovers and the constant hypercover of a monomorphic transition. Added one general Mathlib leaf for local lifting on arbitrary Grothendieck topologies. Restored the parent topology-restriction convention and repaired the false arbitrary-subposet naturality clause; report.md gives an explicit diamond counterexample. Second reading corrected the index reversal in the constant-limit argument using full faithfulness of constant coherent diagrams and the cone mapping-space criterion, and made fibre notation explicit.",
